  "name": "Trippie Redd",
  "editorial_article": "Born Michael Lamar White II in Canton, Ohio, in 1999, the rapper and singer emerged from the SoundCloud era to become a central figure in emo rap and rage. He rose to prominence with his 2017 debut mixtape, A Love Letter to You, released by 10K Projects, featuring the double-platinum single \"Love Scars.\" His sound evolved through early collaborations with artists like Lil Wop and Kodie Shane, eventually blending trap with elements of pop-punk and alternative rock. Throughout his career, he has achieved significant chart success, including his first Billboard 200 chart-topper with A Love Letter to You 4 in 2019. His 2021 collaboration \"Miss the Rage\" with Playboi Carti stands as his highest-charting single on the Billboard Hot 100, reaching number 11. Known for his work with producers like Scott Storch and collaborators ranging from Travis Scott to MGK, he has maintained a prolific output that explores everything from hardcore trap to rock-infused reissues like Neon Shark vs Pegasus.",
